, \nI’m having a persistent issue with Grok Bot on Windows 10. \nDetails: \nGrok Bot version: 0.30.0 (Stable channel) \nOS: Windows 10 \nThe problem st\u0026hellip;","visible":true,"closed":false,"archived":false,"bookmarked":null,"liked":null,"thumbnails":null,"tags":[{"id":416,"name":"grok-bot","slug":"grok-bot"},{"id":408,"name":"networking","slug":"networking"},{"id":373,"name":"computer-use","slug":"computer-use"}],"tags_descriptions":{},"like_count":0,"views":14,"category_id":6,"featured_link":null,"op_like_count":0,"has_accepted_answer":false,"posters":[{"extras":"latest single","description":"Original Poster, Most Recent Poster","user":{"id":137314,"username":"OliG","name":"OliG","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/o/b4bc9f/{size}.png","trust_level":0}}]},{"fancy_title":"Grok Bot 0.30.0 stuck on black loading screen on Windows 11","id":170294,"title":"Grok Bot 0.30.0 stuck on black loading screen on Windows 11","slug":"grok-bot-0-30-0-stuck-on-black-loading-screen-on-windows-11","posts_count":2,"reply_count":0,"highest_post_number":5,"image_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/b/4/b4eb063cf9bbea1045786430dc05f250e4909e7d_2_1023x661.png","created_at":"2026-09-02T06:27:41.196Z","last_posted_at":"2026-09-02T09:12:03.244Z","bumped":true,"bumped_at":"2026-09-02T09:12:03.244Z","archetype":"regular","unseen":false,"pinned":false,"unpinned":null,"excerpt":"Where does the bug appear (feature/product)?\nGrok Bot \nDescribe the Bug\nGrok Bot 0.30.0 on Windows 11 is stuck on a black loading screen with a white spinner and cannot load my Grok Bot computer. \nThe app previously work\u0026hellip;","visible":true,"closed":false,"archived":false,"bookmarked":null,"liked":null,"thumbnails":[{"max_width":null,"max_height":null,"width":1558,"height":1006,"url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/b/4/b4eb063cf9bbea1045786430dc05f250e4909e7d.png"},{"max_width":1024,"max_height":1024,"width":1023,"height":661,"url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/b/4/b4eb063cf9bbea1045786430dc05f250e4909e7d_2_1023x661.png"},{"max_width":1000,"max_height":1000,"width":1000,"height":645,"url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/b/4/b4eb063cf9bbea1045786430dc05f250e4909e7d_2_1000x645.png"},{"max_width":800,"max_height":800,"width":800,"height":516,"url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/b/4/b4eb063cf9bbea1045786430dc05f250e4909e7d_2_800x516.png"},{"max_width":750,"max_height":750,"width":750,"height":484,"url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/b/4/b4eb063cf9bbea1045786430dc05f250e4909e7d_2_750x484.png"},{"max_width":600,"max_height":600,"width":600,"height":387,"url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/b/4/b4eb063cf9bbea1045786430dc05f250e4909e7d_2_600x387.png"},{"max_width":500,"max_height":500,"width":500,"height":322,"url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/b/4/b4eb063cf9bbea1045786430dc05f250e4909e7d_2_500x322.png"},{"max_width":400,"max_height":400,"width":400,"height":258,"url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/b/4/b4eb063cf9bbea1045786430dc05f250e4909e7d_2_400x258.png"},{"max_width":300,"max_height":300,"width":300,"height":193,"url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/b/4/b4eb063cf9bbea1045786430dc05f250e4909e7d_2_300x193.png"},{"max_width":200,"max_height":200,"width":200,"height":129,"url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/b/4/b4eb063cf9bbea1045786430dc05f250e4909e7d_2_200x129.png"}],"tags":[{"id":416,"name":"grok-bot","slug":"grok-bot"},{"id":408,"name":"networking","slug":"networking"}],"tags_descriptions":{},"like_count":0,"views":44,"category_id":6,"featured_link":null,"op_like_count":0,"has_accepted_answer":false,"posters":[{"extras":null,"description":"Original Poster","user":{"id":135686,"username":"Edwin_Cunanan","name":"Edwin Cunanan","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/e/ea5d25/{size}.png","trust_level":0}},{"extras":"latest","description":"Most Recent Poster","user":{"id":87436,"username":"Colin","name":"Colin","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/colin/{size}/90452_2.png","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_group_id":42,"primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","admin":true,"moderator":true,"trust_level":3}}]}],"summarizable":false,"has_cached_summary":false,"valid_reactions":["heart","+1","crossed_fingers","clap","laughing","open_mouth","confetti_ball","hugs","heavy_plus_sign","heart_eyes","sunglasses","cursor"],"accepted_answers":[{"id":488573,"name":"Dean Rie","username":"deanrie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-11T05:57:09.065Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey, thanks for the detailed report. Here’s the key point up front: nothing needs to be re-provisioned on our side. Your account is entitled, your Agent Computer is up and healthy, and entitlement and privacy checks for your account are responding today without errors from Cursor and from \u003ca href=\"http://cursor.com\"\u003ecursor.com\u003c/a\u003e. So there’s no need to use Reset or Recover, they won’t help here.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat we’re seeing: the Grok Bot app on your PC connected normally during the day on September 10, and after that not a single request from the app reached our servers. The \u003ccode\u003eConnectError.Internal\u003c/code\u003e entries are what the app logs when the secure connection is getting cut off on the PC itself, before the request is even sent. Most often, the cause is something on the PC or network inspecting HTTPS traffic using its own certificate. Cursor and your browser trust the Windows system certificate store, so they work. The Grok Bot app currently trusts only public certificate authorities, so it fails. This also explains why your direct HTTPS tests to the Agent Computer hosts succeed.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTry these in order:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIn Edge or Chrome, open \u003ca href=\"https://api2.cursor.sh\"\u003ehttps://api2.cursor.sh\u003c/a\u003e, click the lock icon, then Connection is secure, then the certificate icon, and check the Issued by field. It should say Amazon Amazon RSA 2048 M01. If it shows something else (an antivirus, a security product, or something from your university or organization), that’s the cause.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCheck whether any security software is scanning HTTPS traffic. It’s usually called Encrypted connections scanning, SSL/TLS filtering, HTTPS scanning, or Web protection in products like Kaspersky, ESET, Avast or AVG, Bitdefender, Norton, Trend Micro, Sophos, and similar. If it’s enabled, turn it off or add Grok Bot to exclusions. Then fully quit Grok Bot from the system tray and relaunch it.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIf nothing changes, connect your PC to your phone hotspot (turn off Wi-Fi), then fully quit Grok Bot again, relaunch it, and wait a couple of minutes.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThen tell us what you saw in step 1, whether step 2 or 3 helped it connect, and the name of the security software on the PC. If it still doesn’t work, attach this file: \u003ccode\u003e%APPDATA%\\Grok Bot\\desktop-structured-log-spill.v1.json\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOne more thing: the app downloaded 0.47.0 on September 10, but you’re still on 0.44.0. Once you’re connected again, install the latest version from \u003ca href=\"http://cursor.com/download/bot\" class=\"inline-onebox\"\u003eCursor · Download Grok Bot\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":5,"topic_id":171308,"url":"/t/grok-bot-0-44-0-windows-can-t-reach-computer-entitlement-read-connecterror-internal-please-re-provision-agent-computer/171308/5","accepter_name":"Dean Rie","accepter_username":"deanrie"}],"has_accepted_answer":true,"can_create_shared_issue":false,"shared_issue_visible":false,"can_vote":false,"vote_count":0,"user_voted":false,"discourse_zendesk_plugin_zendesk_id":null,"discourse_zendesk_plugin_zendesk_url":"https://your-url.zendesk.com/agent/tickets/","details":{"can_edit":false,"notification_level":1,"participants":[{"id":750,"username":"deanrie","name":"Dean Rie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","post_count":2,"primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_color":"","flair_bg_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"admin":true,"moderator":true,"trust_level":4},{"id":137263,"username":"Catty","name":"Catty","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/c/e19b73/{size}.png","post_count":2,"primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"trust_level":0}],"created_by":{"id":137263,"username":"Catty","name":"Catty","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/c/e19b73/{size}.png"},"last_poster":{"id":750,"username":"deanrie","name":"Dean Rie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png"}},"bookmarks":[]}